<HandoverLayout title="Operations and access" description="Transfer account ownership, scheduled automation, Microsoft workspaces and evidence intake.">
  <h2 id="ownership">Accounts, ownership and restricted operational handoff</h2>
  <p>AWS hosting is intended to sit in OPDA's account. The receiving owner must verify organisational ownership, billing responsibility, administrative recovery and their own access. This repository review does not establish those facts. Main infrastructure is in <code>eu-west-2</code>; certificate/edge resources also use <code>us-east-1</code>.</p>
  <table>
    <caption>Access transfer register — owners and acceptance evidence to confirm</caption>
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Service</th><th scope="col">Restricted handoff</th><th scope="col">Acceptance evidence</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>GitHub and repository</td><td>Organisation/repository owner, maintainer/deputy, Actions permissions, repository variables, environment controls and recovery.</td><td>Successor can clone, review, commit on <code>main</code> and observe an authorised CI release with their own access.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>AWS and public domain</td><td>OPDA account/billing owner, approved SSO profile, role assignments, OIDC trust, stack inventory, domain/registrar and DNS owners, certificate renewal and alert recipients.</td><td>Expected identity and permissions verified; billing/domain ownership confirmed; operational dashboards and release outputs visible.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Identity, sessions and comments</td><td>Identity-provider ownership, app registrations, session service operations, comment moderation, container registry, database persistence and recovery.</td><td>Approved test user can use the intended participation journey; unauthorised access fails; moderator and recovery responsibilities are accepted.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Microsoft 365</td><td>Tenant administrators, Team owners/deputies, SharePoint site/group/folder administrators, application permissions, automation identity, certificate-expiry monitoring and receipt-key custody.</td><td>Live memberships and organisation isolation read back; a permitted contributor can reach the right workspace and an unrelated organisation cannot; renewal and receipt-recovery owners confirmed.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Teams approval bot</td><td>Bot/app registration and secret owner, installed app, approver-group authority, connector configuration, deployment flag, queues and support responsibility.</td><td>Current configuration read back; authorised decision journey demonstrated; an authenticated person outside the approver group is refused.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>CRM and outbound email</td><td>HubSpot, Postmark and Microsoft app owners, approved credentials/secrets management, sending-domain responsibility, suppression and delivery support.</td><td>Authorised canary verifies acknowledgement, approval state and delivery without duplicate invitations or unintended participant mail.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>NotebookLM and media</td><td>Notebook ownership/access, subscription responsibility, export inventory and authorised media destination.</td><td>Successor opens each required notebook, follows a source citation and downloads/opens the agreed source and output exports.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Developer and scheduled-agent environment</td><td>Approved native model subscriptions, MCP registrations, local source archive, scheduler host, automation identity and operational checkpoint owner.</td><td>Tools are reachable under successor access; scheduled run and recovery are demonstrated independently of the departing developer's machine.</td></tr>
